The backend now enforces JWT authentication via the Authorization header for all protected APIs.

Objective

Update the existing frontend code so that:

JWT is sent in the HTTP Authorization header as Bearer <token>

All protected API calls use this logic consistently

Unauthorized responses trigger logout and redirect to login

Requirements (DO NOT CHANGE EXISTING LOGIC UNLESS REQUIRED)

Token Storage

JWT is already stored after login (e.g. localStorage.getItem("token"))

Do NOT change how login works

Authorization Header

For every protected API call, include:

Authorization: Bearer <JWT>


Centralized API Helper

Create or update a single API helper function (e.g. apiFetch)

All protected requests must go through this helper

Error Handling

If response status is 401 or 403:

Clear stored token and user data

Redirect user to /login

Do NOT retry the request

No Tenant Data From Frontend

Do NOT send tenant_id in body, params, or headers

Backend derives tenant from JWT

Example Implementation (Reference)
export async function apiFetch(url, options = {}) {
  const token = localStorage.getItem("token");

  const headers = {
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    ...(options.headers || {}),
  };

  if (token) {
    headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  }

  const response = await fetch(url, {
    ...options,
    headers,
  });

  if (response.status === 401 || response.status === 403) {
    localStorage.removeItem("token");
    localStorage.removeItem("user");
    window.location.href = "/login";
    return;
  }

  return response.json();
}

Validation Checklist

 Login still works unchanged

 All protected APIs send Authorization: Bearer <token>

 Removing token causes redirect to login

 Expired/invalid token forces logout

Output Expectation

Updated frontend code using JWT headers

No backend changes

No duplicate token logic

