We need a minimal fix in the existing React/TypeScript frontend.

Problem:
When logging in with a super_admin user, the app still redirects to the normal tenant Jobs Dashboard instead of the Super Admin dashboard.
The JWT already contains role: "super_admin" and is stored in localStorage as token, but the app does not decode and use the role for routing.

Apply the following fix only. Do not refactor or redesign anything.

On app startup (auth initialization):

If localStorage.getItem('token') exists:

Decode the JWT payload on the client side (no external libraries).

Extract role, tenant_id, and email.

Normalize role to lowercase.

Set auth state accordingly.

Add this helper:

function decodeJwtPayload(token: string) {
  try {
    const payload = token.split('.')[1];
    const json = atob(payload.replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/'));
    return JSON.parse(json);
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}


Then, during auth initialization:

const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
if (token) {
  const p = decodeJwtPayload(token);
  const role = String(p?.role ?? '').toLowerCase();
  const tenant_id = String(p?.tenant_id ?? '');
  const email = String(p?.email ?? '');

  setAuth({
    token,
    isAuthenticated: true,
    user: { role, tenant_id, email }
  });
}


After successful login:
Replace any hardcoded redirect like:

navigate('/jobs');


With:

const role = String(payload.role ?? '').toLowerCase();
navigate(role === 'super_admin' ? '/super-admin' : '/jobs');


In the protected route / default redirect logic:
If authenticated, redirect based on role:

const role = (auth.user?.role || '').toLowerCase();
return <Navigate to={role === 'super_admin' ? '/super-admin' : '/jobs'} replace />;


Important:

Do not change routes.

Do not refactor architecture.

Only implement role-based redirect using the decoded JWT.

Always compare using toLowerCase().

Expected result:

super_admin → /super-admin

any other role → /jobs

